<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="022" project="spaarke-intake-pipeline-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>FR-14: Console "Submit as a request" — an uploaded document becomes one request and one run (idempotent per click)</title>
    <phase>1 Pipeline core and first doors</phase>
    <gate>after:013,010</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Adds a BFF endpoint (.cs, bff-api tag) and Console .tsx/.ts code (frontend, fluent-ui tags).</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>One endpoint plus one UI action with canonical references and a closed contract.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>P1-G</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>file-overlap with 020/021 (intake DI module) and 017/024 (EndpointMappingExtensions.cs).</parallel-reason>
    <deps>013, 010</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, endpoints, frontend, fluent-ui, react, typescript</tags>
    <estimated-effort>4-6 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>
  <prompt>Add a Console "Submit as a request" action on an uploaded document that creates one `sprk_servicerequest` (channel Console, requester = signed-in user, owner = owning legal team) and one run via 013's run-submit API, through a new endpoint `POST /api/intake/requests` (body `{ "documentId": guid, "requestType"?: int }`, `Idempotency-Key` header generated once per click). Plain chat upload creates no run.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in Minimal API endpoints, the Dataverse write path, React 19 code pages and Fluent UI v9. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>
  <goal>A BFF endpoint + service creating the request and run once per idempotency key, and a Console action with a confirm dialog that calls it, shows the created request and never fires twice; tests for both.</goal>
  <context>
    <background>Spec FR-14 (a, b), NFR-02, NFR-08. Console upload is a door only on explicit submit; plain chat upload stays interactive. Ownership follows the Front Door rule (`IRecordOwnershipResolver`, ExternalIntakeEndpoints.cs:227-260). "Send email updates" defaults OFF for Console (rule from task 020).</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Intake/IntakeSubmitEndpoints.cs</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Intake/IntakeRequestSubmitService.cs</file>
      <file role="new">tests/integration/contract/Api/Intake/IntakeSubmitEndpointsContractTests.cs (contract) + tests/integration/data-mutation/Intake/IntakeRequestSubmitServiceTests.cs (write path)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/EndpointMappingExtensions.cs</file>
      <file role="new">src/solutions/SpaarkeAi/src/services/intakeSubmitService.ts</file>
      <file role="new">src/solutions/SpaarkeAi/src/components/conversation/SubmitAsRequestAction.tsx</file>
      <file role="new">src/solutions/SpaarkeAi/src/components/conversation/__tests__/SubmitAsRequestAction.test.tsx</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ExternalAccess/ExternalIntakeEndpoints.cs (owner resolution :227-260, create :293) — read only here</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/solutions/SpaarkeAi/src/components/conversation/DocumentPerItemCards.tsx (per-item action on the active document tab)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/solutions/SpaarkeAi/src/components/conversation/FileAttachSessionPrompt.tsx (ChoiceDialog wrapper kept out of ConversationPane.tsx)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/solutions/SpaarkeAi/src/services/authInit.ts (authenticatedFetch :96)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="013" status="pending">Run-submit API (request id + channel → run, idempotent) and door kill switches.</dependency>
      <dependency task="010" status="pending">Request channel, stage, current-run and send-email-updates columns.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>
  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-008">SCOPE = `POST /api/intake/requests`. `RequireAuthorization()` plus an endpoint filter that confirms the caller can read the `sprk_document` named in the body (existing document-access filter or seam); denied or unreadable → 403/404, nothing created.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-002">SCOPE = request creation. The BFF service is the only writer of the request's channel, stage, owner and current run; the client sends only the document id, the optional request type and the idempotency key.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-004">SCOPE = the submit. The `Idempotency-Key` header is required (400 when missing); the first call for a key creates the request and run, and any repeat returns 200 with the same ids (atomic claim, not check-then-set). Run payload carries ids only.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-032">SCOPE = the Console door. Kill switch `Intake:Doors:Console:Enabled` off → 503 INTAKE_DISABLED and nothing created; the UI hides the action when the probe says disabled.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-019">SCOPE = every non-2xx. ProblemDetails with stable `errorCode` (INTAKE_DOCUMENT_NOT_FOUND, INTAKE_FORBIDDEN, INTAKE_IDEMPOTENCY_KEY_REQUIRED, INTAKE_OWNER_UNRESOLVED, INTAKE_DISABLED); no document text.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-012">SCOPE = the Console action UI. Use `ChoiceDialog`/Fluent v9 parts from `@spaarke/ui-components`; choose the element (per-item card, chip or menu item) by `docs/standards/ASSISTANT-UI-ELEMENT-CRITERIA.md`; do not edit `ConversationPane.tsx` beyond one mount line.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-021">SCOPE = new UI files. Tokens only, no color literals, dark mode via the host FluentProvider. Visual direction: the action label "Submit as a request" with icon `SendRegular`; the confirm dialog title "Submit for legal review", body = document name + a request-type Dropdown ("Let Spaarke classify" default, "NDA review"), primary "Submit", secondary "Cancel"; on success a `MessageBar` intent="success" "Request {number} submitted" with a link to the request.</constraint>
    <constraint source="root-CLAUDE.md-§10">SCOPE = this task's BFF changes. State the Placement Justification in the PR (`.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md`); measure the publish-size delta against a fresh master build (total ≤ 60 MB); no new package, no new HIGH CVE.</constraint>
  </constraints>
  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/constraints/api.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/pcf.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
