    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Endpoint definition" location=".claude/patterns/api/endpoint-definition.md">Route group, filter, ProblemDetails.</pattern>
      <pattern name="Endpoint filters" location=".claude/patterns/api/endpoint-filters.md">Document-access filter.</pattern>
      <pattern name="Choice dialog" location=".claude/patterns/ui/choice-dialog-pattern.md">Confirm dialog shape.</pattern>
      <pattern name="Control init" location=".claude/patterns/pcf/control-initialization.md">Tag-mapped; no PCF init here.</pattern>
      <pattern name="Theme" location=".claude/patterns/pcf/theme-management.md">Follow the host theme.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>
  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Load the knowledge files; pick the UI element per ASSISTANT-UI-ELEMENT-CRITERIA and record why; declare RIGOR FULL, tier sonnet, effort high.</step>
    <step order="2">Write `IntakeRequestSubmitService`: claim the idempotency key, resolve the owning team for the caller, create the request (channel Console, requester = caller's systemuser, stage Submitted, send-email-updates per 020's rule), link the document to the request, call 013's run-submit API, store the result under the key.</step>
    <step order="3">Write `IntakeSubmitEndpoints` (`POST /api/intake/requests`) with the filter and ProblemDetails codes; register in `EndpointMappingExtensions.cs`.</step>
    <step order="4">Write `intakeSubmitService.ts` (one `crypto.randomUUID()` key per click, reused on retry of that click) and `SubmitAsRequestAction.tsx` (dialog per the visual constraint; button disabled in flight); mount it on the chosen element.</step>
    <step order="5">Tests: endpoint unit tests and component tests per the criteria; build BFF and SpaarkeAi; run tests; measure the publish-size delta.</step>
    <step order="6">Update TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status cell to `✅ [done]`.</step>
    <step order="7">Document the element choice and deviations in projects/spaarke-intake-pipeline-r1/notes/.</step>
  </steps>
  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the chosen element needs a change to the frozen `WidgetAssistantContract.perItemCards` in `@spaarke/ai-widgets` (`register-document-viewer-widget.ts`), STOP and escalate (shared contract owned by the assistant projects) rather than editing it.</trigger>
    <trigger>If linking the uploaded document to the new request would move it out of the user's session or change its access, STOP and escalate (ADR-034) rather than copying the file.</trigger>
  </escalation>
  <justification>
    <existing>spec New Components and reuse-scan row 11: the only request-create path is the external `SubmitServiceRequestAsync` (CIAM/contact-bound, `ExternalIntakeEndpoints.cs:143`); CAPABILITY-INDEX: no internal request-create row. Console upload today is session-only (`FileAttachSessionPrompt.tsx`, `DocumentPerItemCards.tsx`).</existing>
    <extension>No: the external route binds the caller to a CIAM contact and the external plane's gates, so an internal user cannot use it; the create and owner rules are copied, and the run start reuses 013's run-submit API.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>An attorney or business user in the Console cannot turn an uploaded NDA into a request, so the Console door (FR-14, Phase 1 objective) does not exist.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>
  <ui-tests>
    <test name="Submit creates one request">
      <url>https://{org}.crm.dynamics.com/main.aspx?appid={app-id}&amp;pagetype=webresource&amp;webresourceName=sprk_spaarkeai</url>
      <steps>
        <step>Upload a synthetic NDA in the Console and open it.</step>
        <step>Choose "Submit as a request", keep "Let Spaarke classify", click Submit.</step>
        <step>Check the console for errors and the network for one POST to `/api/intake/requests`.</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>One request and one run exist; success MessageBar with the request link; no console errors.</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Double-click is idempotent">
      <steps>
        <step>Double-click Submit quickly.</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>At most one POST (or two with the same Idempotency-Key); exactly one request and run exist.</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Chat upload without the action creates no run">
      <steps>
        <step>Attach a document to chat and ask a question without using the action.</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>No request or run is created (FR-14 b).</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Dark Mode Compliance (ADR-021)">
      <steps>
        <step>Dark theme: open the action and dialog; no white backgrounds or black text.</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>All colors from Fluent v9 tokens.</expected>
    </test>
  </ui-tests>
  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build and test the BFF</tool>
    <tool name="npm">Build and test src/solutions/SpaarkeAi</tool>
  </tools>
  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Intake/IntakeSubmitEndpoints.cs</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Intake/IntakeRequestSubmitService.cs</output>
    <output type="code">src/solutions/SpaarkeAi/src/services/intakeSubmitService.ts</output>
    <output type="code">src/solutions/SpaarkeAi/src/components/conversation/SubmitAsRequestAction.tsx</output>
    <output type="test">tests/integration/contract/Api/Intake/IntakeSubmitEndpointsContractTests.cs (contract) + tests/integration/data-mutation/Intake/IntakeRequestSubmitServiceTests.cs (write path)</output>
    <output type="test">src/solutions/SpaarkeAi/src/components/conversation/__tests__/SubmitAsRequestAction.test.tsx</output>
  </outputs>
  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">One click of "Submit as a request" creates exactly one request (channel Console, stage Submitted, owner = owning team, send-email-updates off) and one run (FR-14 a).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A repeat call with the same Idempotency-Key returns 200 with the same request and run ids and creates nothing new.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Attaching a document to chat without the action creates no request and no run (FR-14 b).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: no token → 401; a document the caller cannot read → 403/404 and nothing created; missing Idempotency-Key → 400 INTAKE_IDEMPOTENCY_KEY_REQUIRED; unresolved owning team → 500 INTAKE_OWNER_UNRESOLVED with nothing created; kill switch off → 503 INTAKE_DISABLED.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The UI disables Submit while in flight, shows the success MessageBar with the request link, and shows an error MessageBar for each failure code.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Dark mode renders with tokens only.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">BFF and SpaarkeAi build; all tests pass; the PR states the Placement Justification and publish-size delta (≤ 60 MB, no new HIGH CVE). Test scope: cover the stated contract plus the negative cases named above; anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in task notes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>
  <notes>Spec FR-14. `IntakeRequestSubmitService` is reused by 041 (Job B accept) and 044 (MCP submit): keep it channel-parameterised and caller-attributed. Deploy is task 029.</notes>
